{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When building a multi-stage form that has many stages, like so:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"image","src":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/form/main/docs/assets/stepper.png","alt":"Form stepper"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It's common for each step to have its own form. However, this complicates the form submission and validation process by requiring you to add complex logic."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Luckily, TanStack Form provides a way to build out sub-forms that make this kind of development trivial to implement: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<form.FormGroup>"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To use a form group in TanStack Form, you'll use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createForm"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"./form-composition.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAppForm"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to create a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form"},{"type":"text","value":" variable, then reference its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FormGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" component like you would a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Field"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const form = createForm(() => ({\n  defaultValues: {\n    step1: {\n      name: '',\n    },\n    step2: {\n      age: 0,\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\nreturn (\n  <form.FormGroup name=\"step1\">\n    {(group) => (\n      // `group()` here has all of the form-like methods you'd expect like `deleteField` or `insertFieldValue`\n      // ...\n    )}\n  </form.FormGroup>\n)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This becomes much more useful when paired with external state to conditionally render a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FormGroup"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const [step, setStep] = createSignal(0)\nconst form = createForm(() => ({\n  defaultValues: {\n    step1: {\n      name: '',\n    },\n    step2: {\n      age: 0,\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\nreturn (\n  <>\n    <Show when={step() === 0}>\n      <form.FormGroup\n        name=\"step1\"\n        onGroupSubmit={() => {\n          // We can move the step forward when validation passes\n          setStep(step() + 1)\n        }}\n        onGroupSubmitInvalid={() => {\n          // Or handle invalid submissions, just like a top-level form\n        }}\n        onSubmitMeta={{} as SomeType}\n      >\n        {(group) => (\n          // Use `group().handleSubmit()` to submit the sub-form, but not the parent form\n          // ...\n        )}\n      </form.FormGroup>\n    </Show>\n    <Show when={step() === 1}>\n      <form.FormGroup name=\"step2\">\n        {(group) => (\n          // Then, use `form.handleSubmit()` to submit the entire form\n          // ...\n        )}\n      </form.FormGroup>\n    </Show>\n  </>\n)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"form-group-validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form Group Validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form groups have a distinct validation proceedure that we think makes sense for sub-forms:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form groups can have their own validation:"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"<form.FormGroup name=\"step1\" validators={{ onChange: () => 'Error' }}>\n  {(group) => {\n    group().state.meta.errorMap // {onChange: \"Error\" | undefined}\n    group().state.meta.errors // (\"Error\")[]\n  }}\n</form.FormGroup>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Can set errors on sub-fields:"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"<form.FormGroup\n  name=\"step1\"\n  validators={{\n    onChange: ({ value, groupApi }) => ({\n      group: value.name === 'error' ? 'Group error' : undefined,\n      fields: {\n        // Must use the name of the field relative to the FormGroup as the error key,\n        // to stay consistent with how standard schema works with form groups\n        name: value.name === 'error' ? 'Field error' : undefined,\n      },\n    }),\n  }}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"And can even accept standard schemas:"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"<form.FormGroup\n  name=\"step1\"\n  validators={{\n    onChange: z.object({\n      name: z.string().min(2),\n    }),\n  }}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The reason we don't use the full path names for fields is so that you can compose your schemas like so:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const step1Schema = z.object({\n    name: z.string().min(2)\n})\n\nconst schema = z.object({\n    step1: step1Schema,\n    step2: step2Schema\n})"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"And pass the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"step1Schema"},{"type":"text","value":" to a form group and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schema"},{"type":"text","value":" to the parent form. That way, partially validated data will still flag errors if the group is bypassed."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"dynamic-group-validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic Group Validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want to use "},{"type":"link","href":"./dynamic-validation.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"dynamic validation ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onDynamic"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with a form group, do not rely on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onDynamic"},{"type":"text","value":" validator passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createForm"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"createForm(() => ({\n  validationLogic: revalidateLogic(),\n  validators: {\n    // This validator will not run `onChange` when a sub-form is submitted;\n    // it will only run `onChange` when the form itself is submitted.\n    onDynamic: schema,\n  },\n}))","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Instead, pass your sub-schema for the group to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onDynamic"},{"type":"text","value":" validation of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FormGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" itself:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<form.FormGroup validators={{ onDynamic: step1Schema }} />","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It will treat "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group().submissionAttempts"},{"type":"text","value":" as the way to change what validator is ran before/after submit."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"form-group-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form Group State"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Just like you're able to access "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group().state.meta.errors"},{"type":"text","value":", you're also able to access the group's value using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group().state.value"},{"type":"text","value":". Likewise, here are some valuable properties you can access in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group().state.meta"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group().state.meta.isFieldsValid"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when the field-level validators have no errors"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group().state.meta.isGroupValid"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when the group-level validators have no errors"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group().state.meta.isValid"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when both the field-level and group-level validators have no errors"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group().state.meta.isSubmitting"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when the group is in the process of being submitted"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"usage","text":"Usage","level":2},{"id":"form-group-validation","text":"Form Group Validation","level":2},{"id":"dynamic-group-validation","text":"Dynamic Group Validation","level":3},{"id":"form-group-state","text":"Form Group State","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nWhen building a multi-stage form that has many stages, like so:\n\n![Form stepper](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/form/main/docs/assets/stepper.png)\n\nIt's common for each step to have its own form. However, this complicates the form submission and validation process by requiring you to add complex logic.\n\nLuckily, TanStack Form provides a way to build out sub-forms that make this kind of development trivial to implement: `<form.FormGroup>`.\n\n## Usage\n\nTo use a form group in TanStack Form, you'll use `createForm` or [`useAppForm`](./form-composition.md) to create a `form` variable, then reference its `FormGroup` component like you would a `Field`:\n\n```tsx\nconst form = createForm(() => ({\n  defaultValues: {\n    step1: {\n      name: '',\n    },\n    step2: {\n      age: 0,\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\nreturn (\n  <form.FormGroup name=\"step1\">\n    {(group) => (\n      // `group()` here has all of the form-like methods you'd expect like `deleteField` or `insertFieldValue`\n      // ...\n    )}\n  </form.FormGroup>\n)\n```\n\nThis becomes much more useful when paired with external state to conditionally render a `FormGroup`:\n\n```tsx\nconst [step, setStep] = createSignal(0)\nconst form = createForm(() => ({\n  defaultValues: {\n    step1: {\n      name: '',\n    },\n    step2: {\n      age: 0,\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\nreturn (\n  <>\n    <Show when={step() === 0}>\n      <form.FormGroup\n        name=\"step1\"\n        onGroupSubmit={() => {\n          // We can move the step forward when validation passes\n          setStep(step() + 1)\n        }}\n        onGroupSubmitInvalid={() => {\n          // Or handle invalid submissions, just like a top-level form\n        }}\n        onSubmitMeta={{} as SomeType}\n      >\n        {(group) => (\n          // Use `group().handleSubmit()` to submit the sub-form, but not the parent form\n          // ...\n        )}\n      </form.FormGroup>\n    </Show>\n    <Show when={step() === 1}>\n      <form.FormGroup name=\"step2\">\n        {(group) => (\n          // Then, use `form.handleSubmit()` to submit the entire form\n          // ...\n        )}\n      </form.FormGroup>\n    </Show>\n  </>\n)\n```\n\n## Form Group Validation\n\nForm groups have a distinct validation proceedure that we think makes sense for sub-forms:\n\n- Form groups can have their own validation:\n\n```tsx\n<form.FormGroup name=\"step1\" validators={{ onChange: () => 'Error' }}>\n  {(group) => {\n    group().state.meta.errorMap // {onChange: \"Error\" | undefined}\n    group().state.meta.errors // (\"Error\")[]\n  }}\n</form.FormGroup>\n```\n\n- Can set errors on sub-fields:\n\n```tsx\n<form.FormGroup\n  name=\"step1\"\n  validators={{\n    onChange: ({ value, groupApi }) => ({\n      group: value.name === 'error' ? 'Group error' : undefined,\n      fields: {\n        // Must use the name of the field relative to the FormGroup as the error key,\n        // to stay consistent with how standard schema works with form groups\n        name: value.name === 'error' ? 'Field error' : undefined,\n      },\n    }),\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\n- And can even accept standard schemas:\n\n```tsx\n<form.FormGroup\n  name=\"step1\"\n  validators={{\n    onChange: z.object({\n      name: z.string().min(2),\n    }),\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\n> The reason we don't use the full path names for fields is so that you can compose your schemas like so:\n>\n> ```\n> const step1Schema = z.object({\n>     name: z.string().min(2)\n> })\n>\n> const schema = z.object({\n>     step1: step1Schema,\n>     step2: step2Schema\n> })\n> ```\n>\n> And pass the `step1Schema` to a form group and `schema` to the parent form. That way, partially validated data will still flag errors if the group is bypassed.\n\n### Dynamic Group Validation\n\nIf you want to use [dynamic validation (`onDynamic`)](./dynamic-validation.md) with a form group, do not rely on the `onDynamic` validator passed to `createForm`:\n\n```tsx\ncreateForm(() => ({\n  validationLogic: revalidateLogic(),\n  validators: {\n    // This validator will not run `onChange` when a sub-form is submitted;\n    // it will only run `onChange` when the form itself is submitted.\n    onDynamic: schema,\n  },\n}))\n```\n\nInstead, pass your sub-schema for the group to the `onDynamic` validation of the `FormGroup` itself:\n\n```tsx\n<form.FormGroup validators={{ onDynamic: step1Schema }} />\n```\n\nIt will treat `group().submissionAttempts` as the way to change what validator is ran before/after submit.\n\n## Form Group State\n\nJust like you're able to access `group().state.meta.errors`, you're also able to access the group's value using `group().state.value`. Likewise, here are some valuable properties you can access in the `group().state.meta`:\n\n- `group().state.meta.isFieldsValid`: `true` when the field-level validators have no errors\n- `group().state.meta.isGroupValid`: `true` when the group-level validators have no errors\n- `group().state.meta.isValid`: `true` when both the field-level and group-level validators have no errors\n- `group().state.meta.isSubmitting`: `true` when the group is in the process of being submitted\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: form-groups\ntitle: Form Groups\n---\n\nWhen building a multi-stage form that has many stages, like so:\n\n![Form stepper](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/form/main/docs/assets/stepper.png)\n\nIt's common for each step to have its own form. However, this complicates the form submission and validation process by requiring you to add complex logic.\n\nLuckily, TanStack Form provides a way to build out sub-forms that make this kind of development trivial to implement: `<form.FormGroup>`.\n\n## Usage\n\nTo use a form group in TanStack Form, you'll use `createForm` or [`useAppForm`](./form-composition.md) to create a `form` variable, then reference its `FormGroup` component like you would a `Field`:\n\n```tsx\nconst form = createForm(() => ({\n  defaultValues: {\n    step1: {\n      name: '',\n    },\n    step2: {\n      age: 0,\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\nreturn (\n  <form.FormGroup name=\"step1\">\n    {(group) => (\n      // `group()` here has all of the form-like methods you'd expect like `deleteField` or `insertFieldValue`\n      // ...\n    )}\n  </form.FormGroup>\n)\n```\n\nThis becomes much more useful when paired with external state to conditionally render a `FormGroup`:\n\n```tsx\nconst [step, setStep] = createSignal(0)\nconst form = createForm(() => ({\n  defaultValues: {\n    step1: {\n      name: '',\n    },\n    step2: {\n      age: 0,\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\nreturn (\n  <>\n    <Show when={step() === 0}>\n      <form.FormGroup\n        name=\"step1\"\n        onGroupSubmit={() => {\n          // We can move the step forward when validation passes\n          setStep(step() + 1)\n        }}\n        onGroupSubmitInvalid={() => {\n          // Or handle invalid submissions, just like a top-level form\n        }}\n        onSubmitMeta={{} as SomeType}\n      >\n        {(group) => (\n          // Use `group().handleSubmit()` to submit the sub-form, but not the parent form\n          // ...\n        )}\n      </form.FormGroup>\n    </Show>\n    <Show when={step() === 1}>\n      <form.FormGroup name=\"step2\">\n        {(group) => (\n          // Then, use `form.handleSubmit()` to submit the entire form\n          // ...\n        )}\n      </form.FormGroup>\n    </Show>\n  </>\n)\n```\n\n## Form Group Validation\n\nForm groups have a distinct validation proceedure that we think makes sense for sub-forms:\n\n- Form groups can have their own validation:\n\n```tsx\n<form.FormGroup name=\"step1\" validators={{ onChange: () => 'Error' }}>\n  {(group) => {\n    group().state.meta.errorMap // {onChange: \"Error\" | undefined}\n    group().state.meta.errors // (\"Error\")[]\n  }}\n</form.FormGroup>\n```\n\n- Can set errors on sub-fields:\n\n```tsx\n<form.FormGroup\n  name=\"step1\"\n  validators={{\n    onChange: ({ value, groupApi }) => ({\n      group: value.name === 'error' ? 'Group error' : undefined,\n      fields: {\n        // Must use the name of the field relative to the FormGroup as the error key,\n        // to stay consistent with how standard schema works with form groups\n        name: value.name === 'error' ? 'Field error' : undefined,\n      },\n    }),\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\n- And can even accept standard schemas:\n\n```tsx\n<form.FormGroup\n  name=\"step1\"\n  validators={{\n    onChange: z.object({\n      name: z.string().min(2),\n    }),\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\n> The reason we don't use the full path names for fields is so that you can compose your schemas like so:\n>\n> ```\n> const step1Schema = z.object({\n>     name: z.string().min(2)\n> })\n>\n> const schema = z.object({\n>     step1: step1Schema,\n>     step2: step2Schema\n> })\n> ```\n>\n> And pass the `step1Schema` to a form group and `schema` to the parent form. That way, partially validated data will still flag errors if the group is bypassed.\n\n### Dynamic Group Validation\n\nIf you want to use [dynamic validation (`onDynamic`)](./dynamic-validation.md) with a form group, do not rely on the `onDynamic` validator passed to `createForm`:\n\n```tsx\ncreateForm(() => ({\n  validationLogic: revalidateLogic(),\n  validators: {\n    // This validator will not run `onChange` when a sub-form is submitted;\n    // it will only run `onChange` when the form itself is submitted.\n    onDynamic: schema,\n  },\n}))\n```\n\nInstead, pass your sub-schema for the group to the `onDynamic` validation of the `FormGroup` itself:\n\n```tsx\n<form.FormGroup validators={{ onDynamic: step1Schema }} />\n```\n\nIt will treat `group().submissionAttempts` as the way to change what validator is ran before/after submit.\n\n## Form Group State\n\nJust like you're able to access `group().state.meta.errors`, you're also able to access the group's value using `group().state.value`. Likewise, here are some valuable properties you can access in the `group().state.meta`:\n\n- `group().state.meta.isFieldsValid`: `true` when the field-level validators have no errors\n- `group().state.meta.isGroupValid`: `true` when the group-level validators have no errors\n- `group().state.meta.isValid`: `true` when both the field-level and group-level validators have no errors\n- `group().state.meta.isSubmitting`: `true` when the group is in the process of being submitted\n"}
